    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0221" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg133"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Denby.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-18"><hi rendition="#italic">October 18,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 754.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Unclose for your information a copy of a
                    dispatch from the consul-general of the United States at Shanghai, No. 222, of
                    the 9th ultimo, in regard to the reported mutilation of missionaries in
                    Shensi.</p>
                <p>Mr. Leonard has been advised in reply that if any American citizen shall be found
                    to have suffered in that reported outbreak, it was presumed that the matter
                    would be promptly brought to your knowledge and be duly acted upon by you.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>




